    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and it passes. BUILD SUCCESS confirms the whole suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the Owner response to include `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` followed by the owner id. The test POSTs to `/api/owners`, then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink == \"/api/owners/\" + id`.\n\nSince the DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI contract at build time and populated by MapStruct, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `id` and the other derived fields), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(toSelfLink(owner))\")` plus a `toSelfLink` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (and `null` when the id isn't assigned yet, matching the existing convention where absent derived values are omitted).\n\nThis follows the repo's established pattern for read-only derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, etc.). `AcceptanceTest` passes and the full build is green.",
